From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:51:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the DMA requests of S_SPI0

The S_SPI0 node has no "dmas". spi-sun6i then warns at probe that it
cannot request its TX and RX DMA channels and moves every transfer
through the FIFO by CPU.

The A733 manual lists S_SPI as DRQ port 53 for source and destination
in the DRQ table of the DMA controller (13.1.4.1, Table 13-2), the
table of the CPUX domain, which is the DMAC0 that the "dma" node
describes. Add port 53 for both directions, in the order of the binding.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: S_SPI0 gets its TX and RX channels from
DMAC0, and a loopback longer than the FIFO passes at 1 and 10 MHz with
the DMA controller interrupt counting up.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index bd6c014147a8..f4069930b9db 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1925,6 +1925,8 @@ r_spi0: spi@7092000 {
 			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_SPI>, <&r_ccu CLK_R_SPI>;
 			clock-names = "ahb", "mod";
 			resets = <&r_ccu RST_BUS_R_SPI>;
+			dmas = <&dma 53>, <&dma 53>;
+			dma-names = "rx", "tx";
 			status = "disabled";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
